# ============================================================================
# BINARY FILES MUST BE MARKED BINARY
# ============================================================================
# The conflict resolution left this file as a bare `* text eol=lf`, which tells
# git that EVERY file is text - including the trained models, the YOLO weights
# and the dissertation itself. Git then rewrites their line endings on
# checkout and CORRUPTS them, silently: no error on commit, no error on push,
# and a .joblib that will not unpickle on the other machine.
#
# The binary rules below must come BEFORE the catch-all, and the catch-all
# uses text=auto (let git detect) rather than text (force everything).
# ============================================================================

# Trained models and weights
*.joblib   binary
*.pt       binary
*.pth      binary
*.onnx     binary
*.pkl      binary

# Office documents - the dissertation and the overview deck
*.docx     binary
*.dotx     binary
*.pptx     binary
*.potx     binary
*.xlsx     binary
*.pdf      binary

# Media and recordings
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.mp4      binary
*.wav      binary
*.bag      binary
*.db3      binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF or bash fails on the shebang line.
*.sh       text eol=lf

# Everything else: let git detect, and normalise real text files to LF.
*          text=auto eol=lf
